.TH MU2E-SHIFT-SCHEDULER 1 "2026-11-16" "Mu2e Shift Scheduler v1.0.0" "Mu2e Shift Scheduler"
.SH NAME
mu2e-shift-scheduler \- command-line interface to the Mu2e shift scheduler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2e-shift-scheduler
.I solve
\fB\-\-shifts\fR \fICSV\fR \fB\-\-people\fR \fICSV\fR
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIYAML\fR] [\fB\-\-target\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-min\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-max\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-alpha\fR \fIF\fR] [\fB\-\-out\fR \fIFILE\fR]
.br
.B mu2e-shift-scheduler
.I serve
[\fB\-\-host\fR \fIHOST\fR] [\fB\-\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR]
.br
.B mu2e-shift-scheduler
.I collab-sync
[\fB\-\-full\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-status\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
[\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fIURL\fR] [\fB\-\-token\-file\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fISEC\fR] [\fB\-\-phones\fR|\fB\-\-no\-phones\fR]
[\fB\-\-members\-only\fR|\fB\-\-all\-accounts\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Console entry point installed by the package (\fIpyproject.toml\fR); it is
equivalent to running
.IR "python cli.py" .
The
.I solve
subcommand runs the two-pass ILP solver over a shifts CSV and a people CSV and
writes assignments; the
.I serve
subcommand starts the web interface; the
.I collab-sync
subcommand copies the Mu2e Collaboration member directory into the
application database. Run each subcommand with
.B \-\-help
for the full option list.
.SH COLLAB-SYNC
Reads
.I /api/v1/users/
from the collaboration site with a bearer token (GET only) and upserts every
record into the
.B collab_members
table of
.BR APP_DB_PATH .
Without
.B \-\-full
only records changed since the last successful run are fetched
.RB ( updated_since );
the run's start time becomes the next
.B updated_since
only when the whole run succeeds. Records with a
.B schema_version
newer than 1 abort the run without writing. With phone lookups enabled and an
admin-owned token, each fetched record is also read with
.B ?detail=full
for office and mobile phones. The run takes the same single-writer lease as
the web application's periodic sync and exits 3 when another sync holds it.
.TP
.B \-\-full
Ignore
.B updated_since
and fetch every record.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Fetch and validate, write nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Print the effective configuration (token redacted), last sync status and
record counts as JSON; no fetch.
.TP
.BI \-\-token\-file " PATH"
File holding the token; overrides
.BR MU2E_COLLAB_TOKEN .
.PP
Configuration precedence: command line > environment (and
.I .env
via the start script) > the
.B collaboration:
section of
.I config/config.yaml
> defaults. Environment variables:
.BR MU2E_COLLAB_URL ,
.BR MU2E_COLLAB_TOKEN ,
.BR MU2E_COLLAB_TOKEN_FILE ,
.B MU2E_COLLAB_SYNC_HOURS
(periodic in-app sync, 0 disables),
.BR MU2E_COLLAB_FETCH_PHONES ,
.BR MU2E_COLLAB_MEMBERS_ONLY ,
.BR MU2E_COLLAB_TIMEOUT .
.PP
Exit status: 0 success, 1 sync failed (message on stderr), 2 no token,
3 lease held by another sync.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
mu2e-shift-scheduler collab-sync \-\-token\-file mu2e-collaboration-api-access-token \-\-full
mu2e-shift-scheduler collab-sync \-\-status
MU2E_COLLAB_TOKEN_FILE=/run/secrets/collab mu2e-shift-scheduler collab-sync \-\-json
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start-mu2e-shift-scheduler (1),
.BR create-shift-blocks (1)
